WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.881 --> 00:00:13.926
Previously on Dead City.

2
00:00:14.101 --> 00:00:15.817
With the methane.
we can bring the city back.

3
00:00:15.841 --> 00:00:16.973
Right around the time

4
00:00:17.104 --> 00:00:18.627
that the world turned into shit soup.

5
00:00:18.757 --> 00:00:21.064
The Croat showed up at my door.

6
00:00:21.195 --> 00:00:24.067
Said that I made him feel safe.

7
00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:26.287
He murdered your husband.

8
00:00:29.464 --> 00:00:32.075
Just look after Ginny. will ya?

9
00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:33.511
No!

10
00:00:33.642 --> 00:00:35.774
Our world has been destroyed.

11
00:00:36.558 --> 00:00:38.995
So now. we get to build something new.

12
00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.759
Hey. who are you?
You're not supposed to be here.

13
00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:06.501
Do you hear that?

14
00:01:06.849 --> 00:01:09.156
Maybe we should get in there.

15
00:01:09.286 --> 00:01:14.074
No... Sarge told us to hang
these up all around. come on.

16
00:01:14.639 --> 00:01:15.640
Lead the way.

17
00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:18.730
You lead the way.
Always tellin' me what to do.

18
00:02:20.096 --> 00:02:21.663
What the hell are you doing?

19
00:02:25.014 --> 00:02:26.146
You were sleeping.

20
00:02:26.798 --> 00:02:28.452
Armstrong and I got to talking.

21
00:02:28.583 --> 00:02:31.890
She was my responsibility. Mine!

22
00:02:32.413 --> 00:02:35.938
I was... I was tryin' to do you a favor.

23
00:02:36.025 --> 00:02:37.437
You're still healing from the wound.

24
00:02:37.461 --> 00:02:39.463
Where you stabbed me
in the goddamn back?

25
00:02:40.508 --> 00:02:41.668
Never ends with you. does it?

26
00:02:42.945 --> 00:02:45.426
First. you lure me
to this goddamn island.

27
00:02:45.513 --> 00:02:46.731
and then you lie to me.

28
00:02:47.515 --> 00:02:49.734
and then you hand me over
to some psychopath

29
00:02:49.865 --> 00:02:51.538
because you think you're
gonna get your son back.

30
00:02:51.562 --> 00:02:54.739
But you don't get your son back
because he sees the psychopath

31
00:02:54.826 --> 00:02:56.350
as the mama you'll never be.

32
00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.481
Don't.

33
00:02:57.916 --> 00:02:59.198
Doesn't end there. though. does it?

34
00:02:59.222 --> 00:03:00.571
No.

35
00:03:00.702 --> 00:03:03.095
Why don't you try murdering me
as the cherry on top

36
00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.576
of your shit sundae of shit ideas

37
00:03:05.663 --> 00:03:07.839
and pretend you don't torch
everything you touch

38
00:03:08.275 --> 00:03:09.624
by burying the one person

39
00:03:09.711 --> 00:03:11.297
- on this godforsaken island...
- Listen to me!

40
00:03:11.321 --> 00:03:12.322
I am sorry.

41
00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:17.936
I'm sorry for what I did.
I'm sorry for what you lost.

42
00:03:19.024 --> 00:03:21.331
If I could undo anything
that's been done. I would.

43
00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:23.680
Would you?

44
00:03:25.117 --> 00:03:27.119
This... This is where we are.

45
00:03:27.946 --> 00:03:29.948
And we can either keep rehashing
all this shit

46
00:03:30.035 --> 00:03:31.875
that we can't change.
or we can try to move on.

47
00:03:33.256 --> 00:03:35.911
I have nothin' to move on to
thanks to you.

48
00:03:39.697 --> 00:03:41.351
I'm stayin' put for Hershel.

49
00:03:44.093 --> 00:03:45.834
You got nothin'
and no one to stay put for.

50
00:03:45.921 --> 00:03:48.010
So why don't you go?
I'll help you pack your bags.

51
00:03:51.535 --> 00:03:52.535
Who are you kiddin'?

52
00:03:54.668 --> 00:03:55.844
You're never gonna let me go.

53
00:03:57.672 --> 00:04:00.196
All I am to you. all I ever will be...

54
00:04:01.632 --> 00:04:04.374
is a big old shit pile of the shittiest shit

55
00:04:04.505 --> 00:04:05.767
that I have ever done.

56
00:04:06.855 --> 00:04:07.943
The fact of the matter is.

57
00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.511
you need someone as shitty as me

58
00:04:10.598 --> 00:04:12.556
because I am
the only person shitty enough

59
00:04:12.643 --> 00:04:16.386
to make you feel less shitty
about your shit pile of a life.

60
00:04:16.517 --> 00:04:18.837
So do me a favor and go ahead
and keep twistin' that knife.

61
00:04:18.867 --> 00:04:21.826
because we both know
that is the one goddamn thing

62
00:04:21.957 --> 00:04:23.357
that you'll do without screwin' up.

63
00:04:24.351 --> 00:04:28.790
Okay. then you fucking stab me.
Take it. Clean slate. Let's go.

64
00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:31.532
Here.

65
00:04:32.446 --> 00:04:33.838
I don't wanna die. okay?

66
00:04:33.925 --> 00:04:35.947
But I will gladly bleed a little
if it'll make you shut

67
00:04:35.971 --> 00:04:37.451
that gapin' bullshit hole.

68
00:04:37.581 --> 00:04:40.628
So either do it or for the love
of God. shut the fuck up.

69
00:04:42.456 --> 00:04:43.370
It is a one-time offer

70
00:04:43.457 --> 00:04:44.893
with a ten-second expiration date.

71
00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:47.287
so you better get to it... Ten.

72
00:04:47.635 --> 00:04:50.377
- Nine. eight. seven. six...
- You are batshit.

73
00:04:51.029 --> 00:04:53.597
Probably... Five. four...

74
00:04:53.945 --> 00:04:55.207
- Three...
- I'm gonna do it.

75
00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:58.558
- Do it! Two. one...
- Drop your weapons!

76
00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.304
She said drop your weapons!

77
00:05:06.001 --> 00:05:08.960
- You got bullets in those guns?
- You wanna find out?

78
00:05:12.094 --> 00:05:13.313
And whatever the hell that is.

79
00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.796
What is this. all right?
What do you want?

80
00:05:20.537 --> 00:05:22.365
We were on our way to the cathedral

81
00:05:22.496 --> 00:05:23.627
to steal a methane tank.

82
00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:25.367
Heard you call him Negan.

83
00:05:27.675 --> 00:05:31.461
Rumor has it that's the name
of the Croat's #2.

84
00:05:33.028 --> 00:05:34.508
With your boy here as leverage?

85
00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.975
Our plan just got a hell of a lot easier.

86
00:05:37.206 --> 00:05:38.206
My boy?

87
00:05:39.251 --> 00:05:40.340
He just had a knife on me.

88
00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.037
I've got nothin' to do with this.

89
00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:43.343
She's lyin'.

90
00:05:43.473 --> 00:05:45.214
She is definitely the Croat's #3.

91
00:05:45.301 --> 00:05:46.128
Listen to me. You...

92
00:05:46.258 --> 00:05:47.258
Both of you. shut up!

93
00:05:47.477 --> 00:05:48.478
Go!

94
00:05:48.783 --> 00:05:49.783
You are makin' a mistake.

95
00:05:51.089 --> 00:05:52.090
The Croat is in the wind.

96
00:05:52.177 --> 00:05:53.537
It's New Babylon who's got control

97
00:05:53.614 --> 00:05:55.093
of those methane tanks now.

98
00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.661
So if you want us to get close.
any of us. we get hanged:

99
00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:00.055
you. us. all of us.

100
00:06:02.449 --> 00:06:04.842
Bullshit. Get walking.

101
00:06:05.887 --> 00:06:07.715
- Go.
- Come on. Come on.

102
00:06:13.242 --> 00:06:14.939
- Alley on your right.
- Clear.

103
00:06:18.726 --> 00:06:20.554
Is he your brother?
I see the resemblance.

104
00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:26.386
Yeah. He yours?

105
00:06:27.778 --> 00:06:30.041
No. Definitely no.

106
00:06:30.955 --> 00:06:32.522
Well. you sure as hell fight like it.

107
00:06:33.654 --> 00:06:34.742
Cellar door on your left.

108
00:06:35.569 --> 00:06:36.569
Looks clear.

109
00:06:36.961 --> 00:06:39.573
Mom? Mom?!

110
00:06:40.095 --> 00:06:42.227
- Hershel?
- Mom!

111
00:08:01.219 --> 00:08:02.786
All the dead in this city are going

112
00:08:02.873 --> 00:08:04.962
to be coming this way
after that explosion.

113
00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.311
We need to find cover.

114
00:08:07.487 --> 00:08:08.575
We need to find Negan.

115
00:08:34.338 --> 00:08:37.778
Hershel! Hershel. where are you?

116
00:08:38.561 --> 00:08:39.909
Hershel. down here!

117
00:08:40.911 --> 00:08:41.932
Hershel! Can you hear me?!

118
00:08:41.956 --> 00:08:43.392
Mom?

119
00:08:49.441 --> 00:08:50.486
Hershel!

120
00:09:01.845 --> 00:09:03.368
I'm sorry for this.

121
00:09:03.455 --> 00:09:06.850
For what?

122
00:09:06.937 --> 00:09:09.592
That.

123
00:09:10.332 --> 00:09:12.595
God. I so should've stabbed you.

124
00:09:55.812 --> 00:09:59.773
Luis! Luis. you look terrible. my friend.

125
00:10:01.426 --> 00:10:02.863
You're gonna lead us to the tanks.

126
00:10:04.038 --> 00:10:07.737
You're gonna give us one.
and then you're going to die.

127
00:10:17.268 --> 00:10:18.268
The tanks?

128
00:10:18.966 --> 00:10:20.750
What do you think that explosion was?

129
00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:23.448
Tanks are gone.

130
00:10:24.624 --> 00:10:27.627
- What?
- What I created?

131
00:10:28.715 --> 00:10:32.414
Falling into the hands of
those... New Babylon Visigoths?

132
00:10:33.415 --> 00:10:36.810
No. They had to be exploded.

133
00:10:37.941 --> 00:10:39.160
Then you'll make us one.

134
00:10:41.771 --> 00:10:43.599
There won't be time enough for that.

135
00:11:00.529 --> 00:11:04.402
No. Luis! No. no. Come on.

136
00:11:04.489 --> 00:11:06.666
It's not worth it. Luis...

137
00:11:52.799 --> 00:11:54.017
All right. dickhead.

138
00:11:55.323 --> 00:11:56.716
I guess you get the honor.

139
00:12:04.462 --> 00:12:07.683
- Mom!? Are you down here?
- Over here!

140
00:12:11.208 --> 00:12:14.777
Hershel...

141
00:12:14.864 --> 00:12:16.736
- Where's your wrists?
- God.

142
00:12:28.312 --> 00:12:30.750
Luis. it is not safe out here.
We need cover.

143
00:12:33.317 --> 00:12:36.712
There!

144
00:12:47.375 --> 00:12:48.375
What are you doin'?

145
00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.160
Renata...

146
00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.295
Damn it. leave him!

147
00:12:57.864 --> 00:12:59.039
Shit!

148
00:13:16.273 --> 00:13:18.536
Negan!

149
00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:23.498
I had a feeling our paths would
cross again before the end.

150
00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:24.890
You.

151
00:13:30.026 --> 00:13:32.289
No. no! Stop. stop. stop. stop! Please.

152
00:13:32.812 --> 00:13:33.852
We weren't gonna hurt you.

153
00:13:34.335 --> 00:13:36.685
We were just tryin' to keep a baby alive.

154
00:14:01.014 --> 00:14:03.407
Yvette. the kids wanna
show you the stuffy they made

155
00:14:03.494 --> 00:14:05.018
for the baby.

156
00:14:05.105 --> 00:14:06.343
Aww. It better not make me cry.

157
00:14:06.367 --> 00:14:09.892
Aw. see. Tio Chucho loves it.

158
00:14:09.979 --> 00:14:11.579
As if the world
weren't fucked up enough.

159
00:14:11.633 --> 00:14:13.785
now there's gonna be a little
Chucho runnin' around here?

160
00:14:13.809 --> 00:14:14.809
Can't believe it. dude.

161
00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:16.680
I love you. bro.

162
00:14:18.858 --> 00:14:19.858
I love you. man.

163
00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:28.389
No. no. no. no.
Don't stop on my account.

164
00:14:29.172 --> 00:14:30.652
You have much to celebrate.

165
00:14:32.436 --> 00:14:38.312
My eyes and ears tell me
your family is expanding. yes?

166
00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:41.271
Yes.

167
00:14:42.055 --> 00:14:43.495
Yvette and Chucho are having a baby.

168
00:14:44.144 --> 00:14:45.144
Well. then.

169
00:14:45.972 --> 00:14:48.888
I suppose congratulations are in order.

170
00:14:50.672 --> 00:14:56.417
Flowers from the cemetery.
And the world begins anew?

171
00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:04.816
And yet. Renata...

172
00:15:05.339 --> 00:15:10.387
all this at the very time I have
an issue to address with you.

173
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.089
We have an arrangement. yes?

174
00:15:18.569 --> 00:15:19.919
We protect you.

175
00:15:23.052 --> 00:15:25.750
With respect. the deal was forced on us.

176
00:15:25.837 --> 00:15:27.622
We didn't need it.

177
00:15:27.709 --> 00:15:30.103
So why don't we just end it?

178
00:15:32.061 --> 00:15:33.933
The Burazi protect this island.

179
00:15:35.847 --> 00:15:37.767
The deal ends when you leave it.
Are you leaving?

180
00:15:39.503 --> 00:15:41.263
Our family's been here
a hell of a lot longer

181
00:15:41.331 --> 00:15:42.331
than you guys have.

182
00:15:46.075 --> 00:15:47.642
Well. good for you.

183
00:15:49.035 --> 00:15:50.471
But the arrangement stands.

184
00:15:53.082 --> 00:15:54.954
And the Dama's vision of the future?

185
00:15:59.306 --> 00:16:02.962
Well. it only succeeds if
everyone contributes something

186
00:16:03.223 --> 00:16:05.616
valuable in return.

187
00:16:07.357 --> 00:16:12.319
And as much as I want to
believe you can... I don't.

188
00:16:15.365 --> 00:16:16.603
I was training some of the others

189
00:16:16.627 --> 00:16:17.628
in emergency medicine.

190
00:16:19.152 --> 00:16:21.284
Okay... Doctors!

191
00:16:22.633 --> 00:16:25.593
Doctors are a resource!

192
00:16:28.509 --> 00:16:31.468
Your brother Chucho!

193
00:16:31.599 --> 00:16:33.514
Is he among your trainees?

194
00:16:36.473 --> 00:16:37.648
He is.

195
00:16:42.392 --> 00:16:43.524
Well. Doctor Chucho.

196
00:16:44.742 --> 00:16:46.005
let me take a look at you.

197
00:16:47.919 --> 00:16:48.920
Come. come. come.

198
00:16:49.486 --> 00:16:52.837
So...

199
00:16:55.797 --> 00:16:58.495
Are you a resource. Doctor?

200
00:17:04.458 --> 00:17:05.633
Yes.

201
00:17:07.156 --> 00:17:08.375
Well. then prove it.

202
00:17:13.554 --> 00:17:17.513
No. no. no.

203
00:17:17.601 --> 00:17:19.646
I've given you a patient. Doctor.

204
00:17:20.778 --> 00:17:21.779
Save him.

205
00:17:22.867 --> 00:17:24.280
Don't leave me. tio. Don't leave me!

206
00:17:24.304 --> 00:17:26.480
Stay with me. Stay with me.

207
00:17:26.915 --> 00:17:30.440
You know... I fear he is not
too good at this.

208
00:17:30.527 --> 00:17:31.876
Maybe you are a bad teacher?

209
00:17:33.965 --> 00:17:37.404
Or maybe you are lying to me
about this whole business?

210
00:17:37.882 --> 00:17:41.060
Don't leave me. tio.

211
00:17:41.147 --> 00:17:43.758
Just look at me. tio. No!

212
00:18:02.951 --> 00:18:04.083
I have no choice.

213
00:18:07.912 --> 00:18:11.699
- You just don't make the cut.
- No!

214
00:18:25.408 --> 00:18:26.844
Yvette...

215
00:18:26.975 --> 00:18:30.587
You know.
I was someone's trainee once.

216
00:18:30.935 --> 00:18:32.372
Hopefully better than Chucho.

217
00:18:33.721 --> 00:18:37.028
And one of the many things
my mentor taught me was

218
00:18:37.116 --> 00:18:38.943
that killing the right person

219
00:18:39.466 --> 00:18:44.949
at the right time makes
everyone else fall in line.

220
00:18:46.429 --> 00:18:48.605
So. I wonder...

221
00:18:51.652 --> 00:18:56.135
Did I pick the right person... persons?

222
00:18:58.659 --> 00:19:00.574
Maybe we should try this again?

223
00:19:02.619 --> 00:19:04.578
Who shall be the next patient.

224
00:19:08.495 --> 00:19:12.716
Eenie. meenie. miney...

225
00:19:12.803 --> 00:19:17.243
Renata... Renata...

226
00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:18.853
Do you really believe one

227
00:19:18.983 --> 00:19:21.856
of those slapdash weapons
can save your family?

228
00:19:25.903 --> 00:19:28.210
Everybody back.

229
00:19:34.477 --> 00:19:35.609
I'm willing to die for them.

230
00:19:37.263 --> 00:19:38.525
Are you?

231
00:19:40.701 --> 00:19:42.485
I don't think you would.

232
00:19:43.486 --> 00:19:44.879
You don't know me very well.

233
00:19:55.281 --> 00:19:59.110
This isn't over. For any of you.

234
00:20:01.635 --> 00:20:05.334
Again... Congratulations.

235
00:20:15.866 --> 00:20:20.219
No. Chucho! No. Chucho!
Chucho. please?

236
00:20:38.672 --> 00:20:41.109
They're closed. but there's no lock.

237
00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:42.478
My sister-in-law is having her baby.

238
00:20:42.502 --> 00:20:43.807
We need to go now.

239
00:20:43.938 --> 00:20:45.742
All right. well.
walkers are swarming out there.

240
00:20:45.766 --> 00:20:47.486
There's nothing any of us can
do about that.

241
00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:52.425
Nobody is going anywhere.

242
00:21:01.042 --> 00:21:02.976
He and I are gonna make sure
that this place is safe.

243
00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:04.282
If you would just let us explain.

244
00:21:04.306 --> 00:21:05.544
The baby is coming two months early...

245
00:21:05.568 --> 00:21:06.648
- Nobody...
- If we don't...

246
00:21:07.918 --> 00:21:10.878
kill anybody until we get back.

247
00:21:34.597 --> 00:21:36.469
There's another door up the stairs.

248
00:21:36.556 --> 00:21:38.471
There may be a way out. but it's secure.

249
00:21:39.298 --> 00:21:40.299
Okay.

250
00:21:42.431 --> 00:21:43.951
- How did you...
- I know Ginny's dead.

251
00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:47.175
You know?

252
00:21:48.437 --> 00:21:49.656
I saw you bury her.

253
00:21:52.963 --> 00:21:54.487
And I went looking for you. and...

254
00:21:56.837 --> 00:21:58.757
Just wanted to see if
you were really gonna stay.

255
00:22:01.102 --> 00:22:02.222
You thought that I wouldn't?

256
00:22:04.061 --> 00:22:05.461
I wouldn't blame you if you didn't.

257
00:22:09.415 --> 00:22:11.330
When I got back. the Dama...

258
00:22:13.027 --> 00:22:14.027
She knew what I did.

259
00:22:14.811 --> 00:22:16.891
She started talkin' about how it
wasn't enough for me

260
00:22:16.944 --> 00:22:18.424
to hurt you.

261
00:22:22.602 --> 00:22:23.603
She told me I had to...

262
00:22:26.475 --> 00:22:28.042
She told me I had to kill you.

263
00:22:30.349 --> 00:22:31.829
Just like how I told you to kill him.

264
00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:36.050
I... I think it came from her.

265
00:22:37.878 --> 00:22:39.706
Just being around her.

266
00:22:42.404 --> 00:22:44.972
And I just didn't see it. And I should've.

267
00:22:45.407 --> 00:22:48.105
No. It's what she does. Hershel.

268
00:22:48.715 --> 00:22:51.848
She sees what people
are looking for. what they need.

269
00:22:52.196 --> 00:22:54.373
and she uses it to get what she wants.

270
00:22:56.462 --> 00:22:58.422
It's easier than you would
think to lose yourself.

271
00:23:01.031 --> 00:23:05.079
And you were right to be mad.
Because I wasn't there.

272
00:23:08.648 --> 00:23:10.389
Yeah. after she told me to...

273
00:23:12.869 --> 00:23:14.829
I started thinkin' about
the times you were there.

274
00:23:17.221 --> 00:23:19.093
the scary things you made go away.

275
00:23:22.836 --> 00:23:24.098
You made it so I had a life.

276
00:23:27.188 --> 00:23:32.280
I don't want to spend it being
mad anymore. at you. at anyone.

277
00:23:34.325 --> 00:23:35.631
Me neither.

278
00:23:50.733 --> 00:23:52.013
She's not gonna hurt us anymore.

279
00:23:53.083 --> 00:23:56.783
I won't let her. We won't let her.

280
00:23:58.306 --> 00:24:00.308
Soon as it's safe.
we're gonna get out of here.

281
00:24:01.048 --> 00:24:03.964
go home. and start over.

282
00:24:07.968 --> 00:24:10.231
Hershel. you're gonna move mountains.

283
00:24:16.193 --> 00:24:17.562
You said Yvette is
only 7 months pregnant!

284
00:24:17.586 --> 00:24:21.024
Luis. how can I help you
with your hand on my throat?

285
00:24:21.198 --> 00:24:24.637
Hey. hey!

286
00:24:26.987 --> 00:24:29.163
Were you gonna do anything
to try to stop this?

287
00:24:29.772 --> 00:24:31.732
No. I'm puttin' the little ball
in the little cup.

288
00:24:34.429 --> 00:24:36.276
This sociopath killed our
brother right in front of us

289
00:24:36.300 --> 00:24:37.824
and our uncle.

290
00:24:37.954 --> 00:24:41.654
Okay. maybe...
Maybe I handled things badly.

291
00:24:43.569 --> 00:24:46.006
But I was just trying to make a point.

292
00:24:46.441 --> 00:24:48.835
- As my mentor taught me.
- Mentor?

293
00:24:58.409 --> 00:25:00.847
You said you would help.

294
00:25:05.895 --> 00:25:11.597
They know the baby needs
an incubator to have any chance.

295
00:25:11.684 --> 00:25:12.859
And a tank would make it run.

296
00:25:13.599 --> 00:25:15.252
You need to show us how
to build one now.

297
00:25:15.775 --> 00:25:16.775
There's no need to build.

298
00:25:18.517 --> 00:25:19.605
There's still a tank left.

299
00:25:21.824 --> 00:25:27.221
There is a single prototype
I hid away a long time ago

300
00:25:29.832 --> 00:25:33.227
with plans and detail how to make more.

301
00:25:33.749 --> 00:25:35.185
Where? Where is it?

302
00:25:36.012 --> 00:25:38.798
And I tell you and he kills me? No.

303
00:25:40.713 --> 00:25:42.889
My story does not end
in a musty basement.

304
00:25:44.107 --> 00:25:48.068
No. I'll show you. It's not far from here.

305
00:25:48.895 --> 00:25:49.895
So we go now.

306
00:25:51.071 --> 00:25:52.420
He shows us where the tank is.

307
00:25:52.725 --> 00:25:55.138
Our family's still waiting at
the hospital with the generator.

308
00:25:55.162 --> 00:25:58.121
I told you. you're not gonna
last five minutes out there.

309
00:25:58.252 --> 00:25:59.795
We don't know how long
he'll last in here.

310
00:25:59.819 --> 00:26:01.124
Luis. she's right.

311
00:26:01.560 --> 00:26:03.387
We are no good to anyone dead. okay?

312
00:26:03.474 --> 00:26:05.738
We wait it out here as long
as we can and then we go.

313
00:26:05.825 --> 00:26:09.393
Listen to her. Luis.
Because what I'm offering

314
00:26:10.351 --> 00:26:12.571
has value far beyond the child's life.

315
00:26:13.528 --> 00:26:14.528
It's my legacy.

316
00:26:16.400 --> 00:26:19.665
Imagine your homes with steady power.

317
00:26:20.491 --> 00:26:23.756
your own fields to plow. fauna to hunt.

318
00:26:24.931 --> 00:26:26.585
all surrounded by water.

319
00:26:31.067 --> 00:26:32.067
This island...

320
00:26:34.375 --> 00:26:35.855
It could be your fortress...

321
00:26:37.770 --> 00:26:38.770
Forever.

322
00:26:42.209 --> 00:26:43.602
We just wanna save this baby.

323
00:26:45.429 --> 00:26:48.476
And we will.

324
00:26:50.217 --> 00:26:51.217
When it's safe.

325
00:26:52.872 --> 00:26:55.309
we could use some good fighters
to help us out there.

326
00:27:02.577 --> 00:27:03.970
You can save this baby.

327
00:27:04.710 --> 00:27:07.495
Haven't you learned by now what
happens to people stupid enough

328
00:27:07.582 --> 00:27:09.149
to have hope in this world?

329
00:27:11.542 --> 00:27:13.327
Look. I'm sorry.

330
00:27:14.633 --> 00:27:16.330
You can try whatever you want here.

331
00:27:16.460 --> 00:27:19.507
but that baby doesn't have a chance.

332
00:27:22.118 --> 00:27:23.163
Wow.

333
00:27:25.165 --> 00:27:26.253
You're a real fighter.

334
00:27:30.779 --> 00:27:31.779
You're right.

335
00:27:45.402 --> 00:27:46.665
Where are you goin'?

336
00:27:48.188 --> 00:27:49.188
We're in a bar. right?

337
00:27:50.756 --> 00:27:51.796
I'm gonna go find a drink.

338
00:28:38.934 --> 00:28:40.022
She's still being that way?

339
00:28:42.198 --> 00:28:44.026
And what'd ya say to her?

340
00:28:44.635 --> 00:28:47.029
Well. have you thought about...?

341
00:28:47.595 --> 00:28:50.729
That's classic Titicaca.
Don't you wish that... okay.

342
00:28:50.859 --> 00:28:52.078
I hear you. buddy.

343
00:29:04.307 --> 00:29:05.307
Hey there. amigo.

344
00:29:10.183 --> 00:29:11.863
Quite the fustercluck out there. amiright?

345
00:29:15.492 --> 00:29:16.755
You wanna pull up a stool?

346
00:29:17.843 --> 00:29:19.018
Me and Cockenspiel's

347
00:29:19.148 --> 00:29:20.828
about to start a game
of Fuck. Marry. Kill.

348
00:29:20.933 --> 00:29:22.333
And Titicaca's bein' a wet blanket.

349
00:29:22.412 --> 00:29:24.719
so we could use a third.

350
00:29:26.982 --> 00:29:29.463
And don't worry.
I made these guys nice and safe.

351
00:29:31.073 --> 00:29:34.207
Name's Dillard. Skunky brewski?

352
00:29:37.427 --> 00:29:38.427
Sure.

353
00:29:40.735 --> 00:29:42.255
I thought pullin' teeth would be hard.

354
00:29:42.302 --> 00:29:44.304
but those nails were a real son of a bitch.

355
00:29:48.003 --> 00:29:49.613
He likes you.

356
00:29:49.700 --> 00:29:50.745
Thank you.

357
00:29:50.832 --> 00:29:53.313
Welcome to the bar.

358
00:29:54.183 --> 00:29:55.228
Cheers.

359
00:30:10.286 --> 00:30:11.810
Okay. That should hold.

360
00:30:16.466 --> 00:30:18.338
You could've left the Croat to die.

361
00:30:19.034 --> 00:30:20.035
You didn't.

362
00:30:21.036 --> 00:30:22.956
And because of you.
that baby still has a chance.

363
00:30:31.003 --> 00:30:34.963
San Lazaro.
patron saint of hope and mercy.

364
00:30:36.443 --> 00:30:37.443
It belonged to my dad.

365
00:30:39.968 --> 00:30:42.057
He always told us that we had a choice.

366
00:30:42.928 --> 00:30:47.367
We could choose the fight
or we could choose the light.

367
00:30:58.595 --> 00:31:01.468
So you can just forgive the Croat

368
00:31:01.555 --> 00:31:03.252
- after what he did?
- No.

369
00:31:03.339 --> 00:31:06.255
Never. Making him suffer...

370
00:31:06.342 --> 00:31:07.782
I think about that every single day.

371
00:31:14.002 --> 00:31:17.484
But once the killing starts.
when does it stop?

372
00:31:26.667 --> 00:31:29.757
You know. choosing the light after that...

373
00:31:31.585 --> 00:31:33.065
was the hardest thing I've ever done.

374
00:31:35.023 --> 00:31:36.111
It still is.

375
00:31:41.290 --> 00:31:43.423
But it's a choice
that I wanna keep making.

376
00:31:45.077 --> 00:31:46.426
Me. too.

377
00:31:50.734 --> 00:31:52.040
Just started.

378
00:31:54.869 --> 00:31:57.785
Maybe when we're done here.

379
00:31:57.916 --> 00:32:00.614
Luis can take a look at Negan's back.

380
00:32:01.049 --> 00:32:03.791
I put a knife into it last night.

381
00:32:06.837 --> 00:32:10.232
You. like. just just started.

382
00:32:17.761 --> 00:32:18.937
Okay.

383
00:32:24.333 --> 00:32:25.769
That is dastardly!

384
00:32:25.856 --> 00:32:27.641
Fuck. that is fresh. Cockenspiel.

385
00:32:29.164 --> 00:32:31.253
He's gonna kill Audrey Hep.
marry Venus Williams.

386
00:32:31.732 --> 00:32:34.169
And he says he's gonna bang
Barbara Bush like a screen door

387
00:32:34.256 --> 00:32:35.256
in a twister.

388
00:32:36.911 --> 00:32:38.130
I gotta ask.

389
00:32:39.914 --> 00:32:40.959
Where are you from. man?

390
00:32:41.089 --> 00:32:43.352
What planet do you come from?

391
00:32:43.874 --> 00:32:45.964
Well. I'm actually from Earth.
I'm from here.

392
00:32:47.356 --> 00:32:49.315
Upstairs studio apartment actually.

393
00:32:49.445 --> 00:32:51.317
from way before shit went tits up.

394
00:32:52.927 --> 00:32:57.497
So you have survived here
alone this whole time?

395
00:32:58.367 --> 00:32:59.367
How?

396
00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:01.500
So. over the years.

397
00:33:01.544 --> 00:33:03.329
folks either cut bait or croaked.

398
00:33:04.069 --> 00:33:05.069
But I stayed.

399
00:33:05.722 --> 00:33:09.378
And I stayed above dirt by
turnin' each floor into a link

400
00:33:09.509 --> 00:33:10.510
in a CLVFC.

401
00:33:12.294 --> 00:33:14.688
Closed Loop Vertical Food Chain. okay?

402
00:33:15.080 --> 00:33:16.405
It starts with the deadies who go slip in'

403
00:33:16.429 --> 00:33:17.589
'n slidin' into the basement.

404
00:33:20.694 --> 00:33:22.783
Here we got those maggoes
maggin' on the deadie...

405
00:33:32.097 --> 00:33:34.137
Then you got the froggies
froggin' on the maggoes...

406
00:33:38.364 --> 00:33:40.444
Of course we got the Turks
turkin' on the froggies...

407
00:33:42.063 --> 00:33:43.543
Chain goes all the way up to coyotes.

408
00:33:43.717 --> 00:33:45.397
which are surprisingly delish. by the way.

409
00:33:45.588 --> 00:33:47.677
But I am happy to pump
the brakes on turkeys

410
00:33:48.113 --> 00:33:49.393
if you're feelin' kinda peckish.

411
00:33:56.817 --> 00:33:58.688
Did baloney used to be illegal?

412
00:34:08.742 --> 00:34:11.223
Infection is spreading faster
than I'd hoped.

413
00:34:12.920 --> 00:34:13.920
How can you tell?

414
00:34:15.226 --> 00:34:16.358
Rising body temperature.

415
00:34:17.402 --> 00:34:19.381
redness and swelling growing
outward from the wound.

416
00:34:19.405 --> 00:34:21.581
And see this pus
and milky drainage right there?

417
00:34:22.451 --> 00:34:23.451
Not good.

418
00:34:24.801 --> 00:34:25.801
What can I do to help?

419
00:34:27.891 --> 00:34:29.719
Use that water to clean the wound.

420
00:34:30.329 --> 00:34:31.809
I'll find something to dress it with.

421
00:34:34.420 --> 00:34:35.899
So you think

422
00:34:36.030 --> 00:34:38.350
with those plans you could bring
electricity to the Bricks?

423
00:34:38.728 --> 00:34:41.427
We got someone there who used
to be a plumber tryin'

424
00:34:41.514 --> 00:34:42.514
to figure it out.

425
00:34:43.690 --> 00:34:45.431
My cousin Solmari's an engineer.

426
00:34:53.178 --> 00:34:54.570
You should come back with us.

427
00:34:56.181 --> 00:34:58.922
I mean. it's... It has been
hard there with the crops.

428
00:34:59.009 --> 00:35:01.751
Really hard... But with power...

429
00:35:03.971 --> 00:35:05.571
it could be a fresh start for all of us.

430
00:35:08.715 --> 00:35:09.846
And I need a fresh start.

431
00:35:17.941 --> 00:35:19.291
So what kinda doctor are you?

432
00:35:21.510 --> 00:35:23.121
Emergency medicine.

433
00:35:24.470 --> 00:35:26.350
I'd been training my brother
before the Croat...

434
00:35:33.043 --> 00:35:34.784
Had to brain my uncle after.

435
00:35:37.004 --> 00:35:41.791
But when it came to Chucho.
I just... I couldn't.

436
00:35:45.752 --> 00:35:47.057
You and your people.

437
00:35:47.145 --> 00:35:49.277
you could come with me
and Hershel to The Bricks.

438
00:35:51.801 --> 00:35:52.801
Thanks.

439
00:35:53.716 --> 00:35:59.026
But this godforsaken city has
been our home for generations.

440
00:36:03.204 --> 00:36:04.204
The Croat's right.

441
00:36:05.380 --> 00:36:06.860
The city could still be our home.

442
00:36:15.347 --> 00:36:17.305
Hey. where's the tank?

443
00:36:19.916 --> 00:36:21.179
Tell us where it is.

444
00:36:22.484 --> 00:36:24.051
No. I'm coming with you.

445
00:36:25.095 --> 00:36:26.358
End where I began.

446
00:36:29.099 --> 00:36:30.231
It's not far...

447
00:36:30.710 --> 00:36:31.830
He doesn't have much longer.

448
00:36:33.060 --> 00:36:34.192
We need to go now.

449
00:36:40.241 --> 00:36:43.331
I know it's not safe out there.
but we need your help.

450
00:36:45.333 --> 00:36:48.380
We should help. At least try.

451
00:36:52.384 --> 00:36:53.384
Okay.

452
00:37:13.318 --> 00:37:15.058
And if I had
spilled the beans on that one.

453
00:37:15.581 --> 00:37:18.627
let's just say a whole boatload
of people would've had diarrhea.

454
00:37:18.888 --> 00:37:20.803
- That is not appetizing.
- It's not.

455
00:37:20.890 --> 00:37:22.414
Shit.

456
00:37:26.374 --> 00:37:28.594
Hello. Mason W. Dillard.

457
00:37:30.987 --> 00:37:32.119
Welcome.

458
00:37:34.295 --> 00:37:36.210
The Croat. he doesn't have much time.

459
00:37:36.297 --> 00:37:38.430
We have to go now.

460
00:37:39.474 --> 00:37:40.997
What's the point?

461
00:37:41.737 --> 00:37:43.957
I know that you think that
baby's dead. but that mother.

462
00:37:44.044 --> 00:37:45.959
I know what she's been through.

463
00:37:46.046 --> 00:37:47.961
I know what she's
going through right now.

464
00:37:50.268 --> 00:37:53.358
We need numbers.
Please. We need you.

465
00:37:53.749 --> 00:37:54.987
All right. well. you need numbers.

466
00:37:55.011 --> 00:37:56.883
why don't you ask my pal here. Dillard?

467
00:37:57.405 --> 00:37:58.580
I ain't goin' nowhere.

468
00:38:05.152 --> 00:38:06.152
I need you.

469
00:38:11.985 --> 00:38:13.552
I finally got my son back.

470
00:38:14.030 --> 00:38:16.206
and I need to know that
I'm not gonna lose him again.

471
00:38:16.337 --> 00:38:18.426
I need to know that things can work out.

472
00:38:18.905 --> 00:38:20.167
They can't. Maggie.

473
00:38:21.647 --> 00:38:24.954
Without you. you're probably right.

474
00:38:27.914 --> 00:38:29.045
I'm tired of bein' angry.

475
00:38:32.614 --> 00:38:33.614
Aren't you?

476
00:38:37.184 --> 00:38:38.794
After it's done. Luis can stitch you up

477
00:38:38.925 --> 00:38:41.971
and you can be free of me.
free to do whatever you want.

478
00:38:42.058 --> 00:38:45.845
I just... I need this
one last thing from you.

479
00:38:49.979 --> 00:38:51.329
Please.

480
00:39:08.650 --> 00:39:09.650
God damn it.

481
00:39:10.652 --> 00:39:12.654
I was just gettin' all comfy and settled.

482
00:39:12.959 --> 00:39:14.395
I really should've stabbed you.

483
00:39:14.700 --> 00:39:15.875
You weren't gonna stab me.

484
00:39:15.962 --> 00:39:18.356
I was so gonna stab you a little bit.

485
00:39:29.018 --> 00:39:31.891
- How much further?
- We're close.

486
00:39:33.414 --> 00:39:35.503
- It's just ahead.
- Ahead where?

487
00:39:36.112 --> 00:39:37.853
He needs to tell us where to go!

488
00:39:37.984 --> 00:39:39.246
I got an idea.

489
00:39:39.377 --> 00:39:41.217
Your mother. she sacrificed
everything for you.

490
00:39:41.944 --> 00:39:44.077
What would she say?

491
00:39:44.860 --> 00:39:47.646
Her legacy. your legacy.
is about to disappear forever.

492
00:39:47.733 --> 00:39:50.213
Come on.

493
00:39:52.825 --> 00:39:53.945
Does anybody speak Croatian?

494
00:39:56.785 --> 00:39:59.222
Wait. I think I know where it
is. Keep goin'.

495
00:40:18.372 --> 00:40:20.287
Okay. we're almost there.

496
00:40:26.162 --> 00:40:27.922
I think we're just gonna have
a seat. Maggie.

497
00:40:40.742 --> 00:40:41.742
Okay.

498
00:40:49.490 --> 00:40:50.796
Sorry... I know.

499
00:41:03.548 --> 00:41:06.812
I was so arrogant.

500
00:41:07.726 --> 00:41:09.336
I tried to lead...

501
00:41:13.558 --> 00:41:14.820
someone who only knows...

502
00:41:18.214 --> 00:41:19.214
How to lead.

503
00:41:28.790 --> 00:41:30.183
Hey...

504
00:42:13.705 --> 00:42:16.316
- Solmari. We got it.
- Thank God!

505
00:42:16.446 --> 00:42:17.535
Through those doors.

506
00:42:17.665 --> 00:42:19.362
She's in the O.R. Contractions are close.

507
00:42:19.449 --> 00:42:20.886
- Take this.
- Can I help?

508
00:42:21.626 --> 00:42:22.626
C'mon.

509
00:42:24.411 --> 00:42:25.891
Evie!

510
00:42:25.978 --> 00:42:27.414
Evie. we're here.

511
00:42:27.936 --> 00:42:30.199
Mira. Solmari is setting up
the tank across the hall.

512
00:42:35.814 --> 00:42:36.934
The baby's head is crowning.

513
00:42:37.380 --> 00:42:39.861
Yvette. I'm gonna need you
to start pushing. okay?

514
00:42:40.470 --> 00:42:42.211
I need blankets. water to boil.

515
00:42:42.298 --> 00:42:43.898
and an extension cord for the incubator.

516
00:42:43.952 --> 00:42:47.782
Okay!

517
00:42:56.748 --> 00:42:57.748
Okay.

518
00:43:00.490 --> 00:43:02.797
Come on. That's a good push.

519
00:43:03.232 --> 00:43:05.060
- Another one just like that.
- Okay.

520
00:43:05.191 --> 00:43:07.672
Push .Good. good. good.

521
00:43:08.629 --> 00:43:12.459
C'mon.

522
00:43:13.895 --> 00:43:14.940
Solmari?

523
00:43:15.027 --> 00:43:16.158
When you're done over there.

524
00:43:16.245 --> 00:43:17.832
I need you to come here
and help Hershel.

525
00:43:17.856 --> 00:43:18.857
Why? Where are you going?

526
00:43:20.989 --> 00:43:21.989
Tanks need methane.

527
00:45:23.024 --> 00:45:25.374
Feels like I finally got my brother back.

528
00:45:27.028 --> 00:45:28.029
I'm so proud of him.

529
00:45:30.858 --> 00:45:32.860
I'm sure he's proud of you.

530
00:45:34.688 --> 00:45:38.170
You're just as responsible
as he is for things workin' out.

531
00:45:39.954 --> 00:45:41.260
for what you chose.

532
00:45:45.481 --> 00:45:47.266
I was thinkin' when I go back
to the Bricks

533
00:45:47.396 --> 00:45:48.746
and get things settled down...

534
00:45:51.661 --> 00:45:54.839
maybe your people and my people.
we could be in business.

535
00:45:58.538 --> 00:46:00.178
Maggie. you should bring
your people here.

536
00:46:04.239 --> 00:46:06.764
Hey. everything the Croat said
about this place is true.

537
00:46:07.503 --> 00:46:08.896
It is a fortress.

538
00:46:10.768 --> 00:46:15.816
The only thing that we are
missing is someone who knows how

539
00:46:15.903 --> 00:46:17.426
to keep things safe.

540
00:46:20.386 --> 00:46:21.953
This isn't my home.

541
00:46:23.476 --> 00:46:27.915
Why can't it be? I'm serious. Maggie.

542
00:46:28.655 --> 00:46:32.964
Give me one good reason why
this can't be your fresh start.

543
00:46:35.140 --> 00:46:38.796
I mean. Maggie. you and me together.

544
00:46:39.753 --> 00:46:42.756
Just imagine.

545
00:46:48.588 --> 00:46:49.937
I'll have to think about it.

546
00:46:52.418 --> 00:46:53.462
I have to talk to Hershel.

547
00:46:55.508 --> 00:46:56.508
Of course.

548
00:46:58.816 --> 00:47:00.296
Nothing's more important than family.

549
00:47:12.003 --> 00:47:13.963
Are you really gonna
leave without sayin' goodbye?

550
00:47:14.744 --> 00:47:15.833
Well. you know me.

551
00:47:15.963 --> 00:47:17.965
Never one to overstay my welcome.

552
00:47:21.229 --> 00:47:22.840
Thank you.

553
00:47:24.667 --> 00:47:25.712
For what you did today.

554
00:47:27.888 --> 00:47:29.672
I wasn't sure that I'd convince you.

555
00:47:32.850 --> 00:47:33.850
Well. you did.

556
00:47:34.808 --> 00:47:35.808
How?

557
00:47:38.856 --> 00:47:41.989
I mean. you... You said you needed me.

558
00:47:48.256 --> 00:47:51.999
You know what happened
this morning at Ginny's grave?

559
00:47:53.914 --> 00:47:55.834
There was a lotta shit goin' on.
you know? But...

560
00:47:57.309 --> 00:48:00.051
I wasn't mad at you for tryin'to kill me.

561
00:48:02.662 --> 00:48:04.838
I was mad at you because you didn't.

562
00:48:11.801 --> 00:48:13.716
Why didn't you finish the job. Maggie?

563
00:48:18.547 --> 00:48:19.679
'Cause somewhere inside.

564
00:48:19.766 --> 00:48:21.855
I knew you were capable
of what you did today.

565
00:48:23.378 --> 00:48:24.553
You better be careful.

566
00:48:24.640 --> 00:48:26.425
You're makin' my head
get all kinds of big.

567
00:48:34.737 --> 00:48:37.088
You know. I don't think
I've ever seen you smile.

568
00:48:38.263 --> 00:48:39.264
It suits you.

569
00:48:45.531 --> 00:48:48.751
Well. you need me again...

570
00:48:49.883 --> 00:48:54.714
- You know where I'll be.
- That bar? Really?

571
00:48:58.413 --> 00:49:00.285
Turns out we might not be goin' far.

572
00:49:01.721 --> 00:49:03.462
Thinkin' about staying.

573
00:49:03.853 --> 00:49:05.420
I think Hershel really likes it here.

574
00:49:08.728 --> 00:49:10.599
You really think you can change it here?

575
00:49:12.514 --> 00:49:15.169
Once we find the Dama.
who's left to stop us?

576
00:50:20.582 --> 00:50:22.193
That's it...

577
00:50:24.499 --> 00:50:29.635
God... God.

578
00:50:37.512 --> 00:50:38.512
Shit!

579
00:50:49.133 --> 00:50:50.743
You poor boys.

580
00:50:53.833 --> 00:50:55.052
You're hurt.

581
00:50:57.837 --> 00:51:01.188
Half of Midtown... is gone.

582
00:51:01.536 --> 00:51:05.845
- There's no one left.
- No. There must be others.

583
00:51:07.151 --> 00:51:09.588
You'll rest. you'll heal...

584
00:51:09.849 --> 00:51:12.417
And when you're ready.
you'll help me find them.

585
00:51:13.418 --> 00:51:14.767
And then we begin again.

586
00:51:16.464 --> 00:51:19.772
Every empire starts with the broken.

587
00:51:26.257 --> 00:51:30.043
Yes. our work is just beginning.

588
00:51:44.971 --> 00:51:46.296
This place is the start of something else.

589
00:51:46.320 --> 00:51:47.539
something better.

590
00:51:47.626 --> 00:51:48.690
We could bring in even more people.

591
00:51:48.714 --> 00:51:51.804
Here we go.

592
00:51:51.891 --> 00:51:54.285
The whole. you know.
New York City thing.

593
00:51:54.415 --> 00:51:55.895
it is starting to feel like home.

594
00:51:59.420 --> 00:52:01.311
You and Renata really got
something here. Maggie.

595
00:52:01.335 --> 00:52:03.859
It's your job to protect this place.

596
00:52:03.946 --> 00:52:06.146
This is what we asked for
when we turned on that light.

597
00:52:10.779 --> 00:52:12.346
We've come to make a deal.

598
00:52:12.477 --> 00:52:14.740
It gets in the wrong hands.
it could be dangerous.

599
00:52:14.870 --> 00:52:17.482
If you were in charge.
none of this would be happening.

600
00:52:19.048 --> 00:52:20.963
- What's going on?
- We're taking our home back.

601
00:52:22.443 --> 00:52:24.793
I'm guessing this isn't
your first suicide mission.

602
00:52:24.880 --> 00:52:26.621
Not hardly.

603
00:52:26.708 --> 00:52:27.753
Look out!

604
00:52:34.499 --> 00:52:36.283
Together. we can do something

605
00:52:36.370 --> 00:52:38.155
bigger than we've ever done before.

606
00:52:44.204 --> 00:52:45.921
- You guys rolling?
- Yeah. I mean. I'm rolling.

607
00:52:45.945 --> 00:52:47.512
Yeah.

608
00:52:48.252 --> 00:52:51.385
After this much time we did a season...

609
00:52:51.516 --> 00:52:53.126
- It shocked us.
- That shocked us.

610
00:52:53.257 --> 00:52:54.867
Yeah.

611
00:52:55.041 --> 00:52:56.825
You fucking stabbed me.

612
00:52:56.956 --> 00:52:58.847
It is a one time offer with
a 10-second expiration date.

613
00:52:58.871 --> 00:53:00.612
so you better get to it.

614
00:53:00.742 --> 00:53:02.111
For the first couple
of years I was on the show.

615
00:53:02.135 --> 00:53:03.571
Lauren can hardly look at me.

616
00:53:03.745 --> 00:53:06.400
Her process as an actor. and...

617
00:53:06.531 --> 00:53:07.851
I just didn't have my glasses on.

618
00:53:08.010 --> 00:53:09.577
Maybe didn't have her glasses on.

619
00:53:11.579 --> 00:53:13.538
Sorry. I thought you were
better on your feet.

620
00:53:13.668 --> 00:53:15.017
Good to see you. too.

621
00:53:15.148 --> 00:53:17.019
And then we started this spin off.

622
00:53:17.194 --> 00:53:19.152
Every scene. it was always so heavy.

623
00:53:19.283 --> 00:53:21.807
There was never a lightness
or a humor to it.

624
00:53:21.937 --> 00:53:24.984
We are quite silly people
in a very dark world.

625
00:53:25.114 --> 00:53:26.942
- And now it's...
- And now we...

626
00:53:27.073 --> 00:53:28.529
- we can do it.
- We get to bring that

627
00:53:28.553 --> 00:53:29.989
in front of the camera.

628
00:53:30.163 --> 00:53:33.297
I'm going to flip you around like this.

629
00:53:33.471 --> 00:53:36.474
and you're gonna fucking
Bruce Lee the fuck out of them.

630
00:53:36.604 --> 00:53:39.259
I'm no help.

631
00:53:39.433 --> 00:53:41.783
In this season.
they actually work together.

632
00:53:41.957 --> 00:53:43.655
Heard you call him Negan.

633
00:53:43.785 --> 00:53:47.615
Rumor has it that's the name
of the Croat's number two.

634
00:53:47.789 --> 00:53:50.052
Maggy and Negan are zip tied
together. and there we go.

635
00:53:50.183 --> 00:53:51.623
- Yeah. and you never see us...
- No.

636
00:53:51.706 --> 00:53:53.534
Under other people's control.

637
00:53:53.665 --> 00:53:54.990
They're at it with each other. but this was

638
00:53:55.014 --> 00:53:57.146
a great way of us being joined

639
00:53:57.321 --> 00:53:59.105
in misery against another force.

640
00:53:59.236 --> 00:54:00.716
- Yeah.
- Let's talk about this scene.

641
00:54:00.802 --> 00:54:01.977
We need to find cover.

642
00:54:02.108 --> 00:54:03.849
We need to find Negan.

643
00:54:03.979 --> 00:54:06.243
One of the cellar doors
leading to the street is open.

644
00:54:06.373 --> 00:54:08.288
Beneath the open door. makeshift slide.

645
00:54:08.419 --> 00:54:11.160
A beat later. Maggie.
Negan tumble down the slide.

646
00:54:13.380 --> 00:54:14.729
The walkers immediately on them.

647
00:54:14.860 --> 00:54:16.490
That was a cool sequence
that was sort of

648
00:54:16.514 --> 00:54:18.187
still being worked out
closer to production.

649
00:54:18.211 --> 00:54:20.431
- It got worked out on the day.
- That too.

650
00:54:21.954 --> 00:54:22.955
You were being so nice.

651
00:54:33.748 --> 00:54:35.639
Originally it's a fight
in the streets. remember?

652
00:54:35.663 --> 00:54:37.554
- And it was the dust.
- You had an eye infection.

653
00:54:37.578 --> 00:54:39.121
- I had an eye infection.
- I had a nose.

654
00:54:39.145 --> 00:54:40.427
- a sinus infection.
- Yeah. and we were...

655
00:54:40.451 --> 00:54:42.453
So we couldn't do the super dusty scene.

656
00:54:42.583 --> 00:54:44.368
We were both like.
"We'll die. you know?"

657
00:54:44.498 --> 00:54:46.108
- Yeah.
- My eye is going to fall

658
00:54:46.239 --> 00:54:47.782
out of my head. and she's just gonna die.

659
00:54:47.806 --> 00:54:49.446
Yeah. and my nose
was going into my face.

660
00:54:49.503 --> 00:54:51.331
I know we seem like superheroes. but...

661
00:54:51.462 --> 00:54:53.420
No. just kidding.

662
00:54:53.551 --> 00:54:56.162
I mean. I believe us for
what it's worth working together

663
00:54:56.336 --> 00:54:59.296
that I'm here doing this.
and then Negan comes in.

664
00:54:59.426 --> 00:55:00.906
I'm sorry for this.

665
00:55:01.036 --> 00:55:03.735
For what?

666
00:55:05.998 --> 00:55:08.000
And cut. Good.

667
00:55:08.130 --> 00:55:09.891
It's the first time we've
seen them really fight together

668
00:55:09.915 --> 00:55:12.526
since season... yeah.

669
00:55:12.700 --> 00:55:14.136
It could have been 11.

670
00:55:14.311 --> 00:55:17.314
- We need numbers. please.
- We need you.

671
00:55:17.444 --> 00:55:19.403
I need you.

672
00:55:19.533 --> 00:55:21.163
I think what sets
the whole thing in motion.

673
00:55:21.187 --> 00:55:24.321
of being able to move forward
is. for herself and for her son.

674
00:55:24.451 --> 00:55:27.149
there has to be a life without anger.

675
00:55:27.280 --> 00:55:29.195
There has to be a moving forward.

676
00:55:29.326 --> 00:55:31.806
The possibilities for this new world

677
00:55:31.937 --> 00:55:33.982
and for us are tremendous.

678
00:55:34.113 --> 00:55:35.680
I really should have stabbed you.

679
00:55:35.810 --> 00:55:37.464
You weren't gonna stab me.

680
00:55:37.595 --> 00:55:39.161
I was so gonna stab you a little bit.
